  "question": "Evaluate $\\tan\\left(\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)\\right)$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "Let $\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)$.<br /><br />Then $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$.<br /><br />So $\\cos\\theta = \\sqrt{1-\\sin^2\\theta} = \\sqrt{1-\\frac{16}{25}} = \\frac{3}{5}$.<br /><br />Thus, $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\frac{4/5}{3/5} = \\frac{4}{3}$.",
